  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustained Access to Safe Water and Sanitation for Rural Communities in Rushinga -Phase2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to increase equitable and sustainable access and use of safe water and sanitation facilities for 4,161 marginalized people in rural communities of Rushinga District by 2024. The intervention will result in 4,161 people in remote, socially, economically and environmentally marginalized rural area of Rushinga district, having year-round access to safe water supplies and improved sanitation for most vulnerable children at 2 schools. Within vulnerable groups, women will benefit the most, reducing time invested in fetching water, mitigating safeguarding risks associated with the task, improving overall health and hygiene, and reducing intra-household conflict linked with scarcity of water.</narrative>
  </description>
